0..76 Comment "// A returner\'s row may stay open through a row variable, an implicit of the"
77..153 Comment "// kind `Row` (#2270): `log` prints through `Console` and leaves the rest of"
154..229 Comment "// its row to its caller, so one definition is used under every row holding"
230..303 Comment "// `Console`, the variable solved at each call by the row equation, and a"
304..379 Comment "// handler of `Console` takes `[Console | r]` to `[r]`, forwarding the rest"
380..454 Comment "// (Hillerström and Lindley, \"Liberating Effects with Rows and Handlers\","
455..534 Comment "// Type-Driven Development 2016, § 2.5 and § 3.3, T-HANDLER). What refuses is"
535..589 Comment "// in `../../pathological/control/row-variable.gandr`."
591..663 Comment "/// A line printed through `Console`, the rest of the row left open: `r`"
664..716 Comment "/// lacks `Console`, which the row writes beside it."
